    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.92–0.97 from 6 h onward, with a sharp stop after a steep exponential rise. That pattern fits detector saturation. At 18 h, the 10x dilution read 0.481, which scales to about 4.8. The 40x dilution read 0.114, which scales to about 4.6. The two scaled values roughly agree, and the 40x value is the more reliable one because it sits in the more linear range. Both are about 5 times the undiluted reading of 0.92. So the true late biomass is about 4.6 OD-equivalent, and the undiluted readings underestimate it."
